# TikTok Clone — Cursor AI Rules

This project uses **modular Cursor rules** in `.cursor/rules/`. Each `.mdc` file covers a specific domain.

## Rule Files

| File | Scope | Description |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `project-best-practices.mdc` | `**/*` (Always) | Architecture overview, cross-cutting concerns, version conflict detection, naming conventions |
| `frontend.mdc` | `frontend/**/*.ts,tsx,css` | Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui, Redux Toolkit, React Query |
| `backend.mdc` | `backend/**/*.php` | Laravel 11, PHP 8.4, Service-Repository pattern, Eloquent, Kafka, API Resources |
| `ai-module.mdc` | `ai/**/*.py` | PyTorch, PhoBERT, training/inference consistency, Kafka worker, FastAPI |
| `ux-ui-design.mdc` | `frontend/**/*.tsx,css` | Video-first UX, mobile-first design, micro-interactions, accessibility, dark mode |
| `laravel-boost.mdc` | `backend/**/*.php` | Laravel Boost MCP integration, PHP standards, PHPUnit testing |

## Key Architectural Decisions
- **Frontend ↔ Backend**: REST API with JSON Resources
- **Backend ↔ AI**: Apache Kafka message queue
- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit (client state) + React Query (server state)
- **Backend Pattern**: Service → Repository → Model (never skip layers)
- **AI Model**: PhoBERT binary classifier for Vietnamese toxic content detection
- **Version Conflicts**: `updated_at` timestamp comparison via `check_version_conflict()` helper
